{"cluster_id": "C-1026", "topic": "correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-257"], "canonical_claim": "The archaeology report names concrete evidence-based test-coverage gaps (vol. 06 \u00a75): the `SingleWriterSlot` background renew loop has zero direct test references (`MountLeaseKeeper` is exercised only via synchronous `renewOnce`, so the async renewal thread and its error-latch split-brain-safety path rest on review plus soak) \u2014 flagged High because the P3.1 S13 fence-of-blocked-lease wedge lived exactly in this machinery; `CasGcScheduler` thread pacing/heartbeat cadence is unit-untestable without sleeps and was verified by review only (the P3-B1 wedge was exactly here); async-insert retry row-loss (B139) is parked behind the soak default `async_insert=0` with no gtest; and several `IMetadataStorage` overrides (`createMetadataFile`, `truncateFile`, `chmod`, `setLastModified`, `setReadOnly`, `createDirectory*`) are never driven by any test, though mostly deliberate no-ops.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/00-REPORT.md#L636-L646"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1027", "topic": "correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B015-133"], "canonical_claim": "The reader implementation requires a TLA+ invariant that every object in a live reader pin's `replay(S, tail <= L)` closure is neither condemned nor pruned.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-14-cas-readonly-replica-snapshot-pin-design.md#tla"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1028", "topic": "correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B021-023"], "canonical_claim": "The owner-tombstone change requires tests proving that decommission leaves a present owner object with `retired_at_ms` set, that a competing `putOverwrite` makes the tail abort closed, and that a tombstoned same-UUID owner is rejected by `claimOwnerOrThrow` with `CORRUPTED_DATA`.", "issue_ids": ["T5"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-18-t5-owner-tombstone-design.md#L43-L48"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1029", "topic": "correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["B031-002"], "canonical_claim": "A detector should flag a namespace whose current catalog life contributes no checkpoint or listed objects while a non-current life of the same name has listed objects.", "issue_ids": ["NEW-1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-30-stage-b-critical-checkpoint-review.md#new-1-critical-code-the-third-route-to-a-vacuous-frontier-incarnation-mismatch"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1030", "topic": "correctness", "target": "architecture/correctness", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-407"], "canonical_claim": "The TXN-ONE-PIPELINE design's plan-time audits require a fault-injection regression verifying that process termination after a successful `Keeper` publication but before disk `commit` enters the existing missing-part fetch/lost-part path, and explicitly forbid introducing CA-specific recovery for this window.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-15-cas-txn-one-pipeline-design.md#L292-L301"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1031", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-374", "B011-035", "B011-148"], "canonical_claim": "The old `gc_clear_on_spare` behavior and the post-adoption clear modeled by `post_adoption_clear` must remain red in the TLA gate; the latter is specifically unsafe because adoption does not fence pre-CAS side effects.; Moving `clearSparedMeta` after the winning `gc/state` CAS is insufficient because an older leader can execute a stale pre-CAS `deleteExact` after a newer leader adopts a spare and clears the meta.; The first proposed fix for the deposed-leader stray-Clean defect (Fix 1: couple `clearSparedMeta` to adoption by moving it after the winning `gc/state` CAS, plus a `condemn_round` guard) was proven insufficient by a second model consult: a stale, paused leader can issue the destructive exact-token `deleteExact(t1)` pre-CAS from an older adopted snapshot, so a fresh leader's legitimately-adopted post-CAS clear still lets a writer reuse `t1` and the stale leader's redelete kills the live reuse, because the final `gc/state` CAS fences adoption, not pre-CAS side effects.", "issue_ids": ["I1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-11-cas-add-only-meta-fix.md#task-1", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-11-cas-deposed-leader-stray-clean-meta.md#L22-L28", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-deposed-leader-clearsparedmeta-fix-design.md#why-not-fix1"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1032", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B019-124"], "canonical_claim": "The report's earlier claim that `renameParts` performed the CA publish before the Keeper multi is explicitly corrected as false; on CA `renameParts` is only a tmp-to-final overlay re-key.", "issue_ids": ["39cf3279652"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-dataloss-traced-root-cause.md#L63-L70"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1033", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B023-011"], "canonical_claim": "The `lazy_load_tables` proxy is considered unsafe for upstream promotion because it weakens type identity and has roughly sixty unforwarded virtuals, including a silent-empty `backupData` path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-21-storageproxy-forwarding-audit.md#L159-L161"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1034", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B024-067"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS path stages every blob locally and then uploads `pending_blobs` in a serial loop while committing parts one at a time, so one thread orchestrates and waits on each PUT or HEAD in turn.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-23-cas-wide-insert-baseline.md#c-single-threaded"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1035", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B037-090"], "canonical_claim": "The dead-precommit skip was not the S42 cause because `dead_precommits_skipped` was zero on both nodes; the skipped `-1` path never fired.", "issue_ids": ["S42"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-26-s42-stale-edge-repro/PHASE1.md#refuted"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1036", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B041-072"], "canonical_claim": "The previous design treated immutable log PUT as durability even though semantic application depended on later in-memory installation, creating possibly durable-but-not-applied state after an ambiguous PUT.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-28-ref-rework-reviews/codex_simplify_design.md#L17-L20"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1037", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-038", "B043-011"], "canonical_claim": "The intermediate `B167` blob-watermark design had a livelock in which GC could re-condemn a build's fresh upload during the non-atomic upload-to-publish gap, preventing publication forever.; Three B167 build-watermark models (`CaResurrectLiveness.tla`, `CaBuildWatermark.tla`, `CaBuildWatermarkNum.tla`), all removed 2026-07-21, proved that resurrect liveness requires a guard blocking GC from re-condemning a freshly-owned incarnation during the non-atomic upload-to-publish span (the B167 livelock: dedup hit on a stale incarnation is deleted, the fresh re-upload is re-condemned by GC without a guard, looping forever); their safety role fully migrated into `CaBuildRootPrecommit.tla`'s precommit-first reachability mechanism, which replaced the modeled per-candidate blob-guard and condemn-time `HeartbeatGuard` that were never fully implemented.", "issue_ids": ["B167"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#L391-L441", "docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-b167"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1038", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-005"], "canonical_claim": "The B140 dangle was caused by `reuseBlob` (the adopt operation) transferring the blob hash but not the `cas_owner` protection, so an adopted blob's protection stayed bound to the retired byte-writer and GC reclaimed it under a still-in-flight adopter; `system.content_addressed_log` (B170) pinned the precise dangle event with its token and timing.", "issue_ids": ["B140"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/02-methodology.md#L255-L258"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1039", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-006"], "canonical_claim": "An aggressive test GC cadence exceeded the fixed iteration cap of 8 in `resolveAndResurrectGeneration`, producing `CORRUPTED_DATA` failures in ordinary insert/mutation tests; the soak surfaced 33 failures from this single root cause and the fix was a one-line cap change from 8 to 256.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/02-methodology.md#L259-L263"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1040", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-007"], "canonical_claim": "A 2026-06-20 soak reported 1.6M `S3WriteRequestsErrors` and 94 `fsck dangling` after a chaos window; forensic analysis showed all 922,772 GC deletes had `indeg_at_recheck=0`, the errors were ~1.57M by-design `PreconditionFailed` (412) CAS contention on root-shard manifests, and the 94 dangling was a transient read-unavailability false-positive (429/503 load shedding) whose 180s settle budget was too short under write load.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/02-methodology.md#L264-L270"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1041", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-036", "AUDIT-M2-037", "AUDIT-M2-067"], "canonical_claim": "`CaGcIndegRefoldCore.tla` isolated an in-degree-underflow hazard the large safety model could not express: the C++ accumulated blob in-degree as a non-idempotent integer delta stream, which could reach -1 (throwing `CORRUPTED_DATA`) when a completion-seal cursor persisted at the wrong position; the fix adopted an idempotent two-cursor presence-set merge, making the underflow structurally impossible, and the model was then removed because it described a design the code had abandoned.; `CaGcIndegRefoldCore.tla` modeled a bug (H1b) where an in-degree completion-seal cursor persisted at `foldCursor` instead of `max(foldCursor, fenceVersion)` caused a re-fold of an already-absorbed fence-window removal, driving the integer in-degree counter to -1 (`INV_INDEG_NONNEGATIVE` violated, mapping to `CORRUPTED_DATA` in C++); the design decision was that the `Seal` action must advance the persisted cursor to `fenceVersion`, not remain at `foldCursor`.; `CaGcIndegRefoldCore.tla` was removed 2026-07-22 because the shipped in-degree design no longer accumulates a non-idempotent integer delta stream: `CasBlobInDegree.cpp` computes in-degree via an idempotent two-cursor presence-set merge keyed by `(blob_hash, source_id)` where the surviving-edge count is an unsigned integer that structurally cannot go negative, so the underflow hazard the model existed to catch is now structurally impossible.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#L607-L645", "docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#L611-L621", "docs/superpowers/cas/how-we-got-here.md#turn-three-oracles"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1042", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-141"], "canonical_claim": "An external author review of rev.6 confirmed 3 substantive findings: F1 seal-skip-on-empty-dead-region combined with a blind detector, F2 a sticky-boundary-bool causing over-seal plus a fail-open allowlist, and F3 the seal PUT held under `state_mutex` for up to 90s; all three were filed as a fix-round task.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-13-unattended-optimization-round.md#log"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1043", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-297"], "canonical_claim": "`CasInstrumentedBackend`'s classifier still contains a dead `_watermark` classification branch and a stale comment (`CasStore.cpp:263`) claiming the watermark writes a `roots/<server-hex>/_watermark` slot; the standalone watermark object was retired when the watermark was folded into the mount-lease beat by the ack-floor merge (`FormatId::Watermark=7` is retired).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#10-historical-smells-old-terminology-removed-designs", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#9-weak-places"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1044", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-302"], "canonical_claim": "The stage-1 fix-verification pass found the writer-ledger memory regression guard incomplete: `LongTailReplaysUnderMemoryBound` exercises only the free `recoverRefTable`/`recoverRefTableDetailed` path, not `CasRefLedger::ensureRefTableRecovered`, so the ledger's own recovery loop could regress to whole-tail materialization while all existing bounds and the test-local control stay green; a later fix (commit 330d52e8c96) added a dedicated ledger-path test that verifies both an upper and lower peak bound.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-24-codex-stage1-reviews.md#verify-pass-1"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1045", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-331", "B048-046"], "canonical_claim": "Several GC-reclaim tests for abandoned precommits were deleted (not disabled) because reclaiming an abandoned precommit is now the writer's job on recovery (it appends the exact `owner_transition` removal), not GC's.; `GReclaimDeadPrecommit` and `LiveDeadPrecommitReclaimed` are now inert model artifacts because GC-side abandoned-precommit reclaim was removed; the production writer appends the exact `owner_transition` removal instead.", "issue_ids": ["T7"], "sources": [".superpowers/sdd/2026-08-02-cas-stage-b-remaining/t7-laneA-review.md#L77-L115", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#6-contradictions-obsolete-terminology-disabled-duplicate-tests"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1046", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-334"], "canonical_claim": "`gtest_cas_mount.cpp:101`'s comment \"No mount has been written in Task 4\" is stale and contradicts the same file's extensive mount writes; `gtest_ca_wiring.cpp`'s B188 predicate comment still references vestigial `/trees/` though the gate collects only `/blobs/`.", "issue_ids": ["B188"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#6-contradictions-obsolete-terminology-disabled-duplicate-tests"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1047", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-362"], "canonical_claim": "The final whole-branch review (base `d57a41f353d` to head `7771bb60c70`, 38 commits) found a Critical `partAccess` use-after-free (the same class task T9 meant to close but missed) plus a `gcHealth`-blocks-behind-round issue, fixed in `452d17af42f`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-session-full-summary.md#L79-L88"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1048", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-363"], "canonical_claim": "The final whole-branch review found the S22 caller discarded `Committed`/`Conflict`/`Unresolved` outcomes (fixed `8068d8c5fe0`), the decommission owner-tombstone write was not resumable on an ambiguous outcome (fixed `bec89a9de95`), and `emu_token_state` had unbounded growth (fixed `08ea8d1200e`, closing the whole fix-wave and review cycle).", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-session-full-summary.md#L84-L88"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1049", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-364"], "canonical_claim": "S13's quiesce-wedge (cluster died ~6 minutes into the quiescing-cluster phase) was attributed to the same lifecycle-lock class as the final-review Critical `partAccess` use-after-free; after the fix, a re-run with sidecar instrumentation passed 13/13 with quiesce completing cleanly in ~7.5 minutes.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-session-full-summary.md#L171"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1050", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-436"], "canonical_claim": "An early draft of the relink/seam TLA+ model omitted the WedgeRetryCreated action entirely, making the wedge protocol's own happy path unreachable: CasRefLedger.h:784-801 documents that a bounded conditional-create retry either lands the exact same transaction bytes or conflicts, so without modelling that retry as a durability-producing event, WedgeResolveInstall's sApplyOwed guard could never be satisfied and every state downstream of a resolved wedge was missing from the state space.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-29-cas-relink-seam-tla-gate.md#L2132-L2134"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1051", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B005-064"], "canonical_claim": "The mount crash-recovery change does not modify `claimMount`, the owner anchor, the epoch counter, or the watermark, and it adds no user-facing configuration.", "issue_ids": ["S13"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-mount-crash-recovery-design.md#non-goals"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1052", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B009-088"], "canonical_claim": "The no-paranoid-mode decision rejects retaining deleted checks behind a configuration flag; detection remains with ca-fsck, soak assertions, and system.content_addressed_log.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-design.md##deletions"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1053", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B018-029"], "canonical_claim": "The source-layout refactor preserves behavior by forbidding mutex coverage or lock-order changes, construction/destruction-order changes, persisted-byte/key changes, log/event/metric changes, and mixing file moves with content edits in one commit.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-source-layout-refactoring.md#L13-L29"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1054", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-388", "B018-030"], "canonical_claim": "Renaming `Store` to `Pool` and `Build` to `PartWriteTxn` changes only C++ identifiers and file names; the protocol vocabulary `build_seq`, `buildSeq`, `BuildPrefix`, upload stamps, and related build-sequence identifiers remains unchanged.; The source-layout refactor's phase-5 rename sweep (`Store`\u2192`Pool`, `Build`\u2192`PartWriteTxn`) must use word-boundary-anchored seds rather than blanket `s/Store/.../` or `s/Build/.../`, because a blanket substitution would incorrectly hit `IMetadataStorage` and the protocol vocabulary `build_seq`/`BuildPrefix`, which must survive the rename unchanged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-source-layout-refactoring.md#L13-L29", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-source-layout-refactoring.md#L583-L634", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-source-layout-refactoring.md#L670"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1055", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B022-084"], "canonical_claim": "Each `RefTableState` experiment must pass the full gtest and property gates, record benchmark numbers and an explicit elegance judgment, and retain reverted experiment results in the comparison report.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments-design.md#phase-c-experiments", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments-design.md#phase-d-selection"]}

